sqlite: rusqlite 0.41.1 and libsqlite3-sys 0.39.1 (SQLite 3.54.1)

RUSTSEC-2026-0459 (CVE-2026-119375): SQLite before 3.54.0 can return
uninitialised page-cache memory for a database opened with a sibling -wal
file of another page size. libsqlite3-sys 0.39 bundles SQLite 3.54.1 and
needs rusqlite 0.41.

Same change as upstream commit 18757f7e08ec ("chore: Bump the SQLite dep",
2026-11-06): the requirement of matrix-sdk-sqlite and two entries of
Cargo.lock (versions and checksums of the crates.io index; dependencies
unchanged). No source change: the rusqlite API that matrix-sdk-sqlite 0.19.1
uses (Connection, Statement, Row, Transaction, Params, params_from_iter,
named_params, OptionalExtension, ToSql, limits::Limit, Error::SqliteFailure,
ErrorCode, ffi::Error::new) has the same signatures in 0.40.2 and 0.41.1
(read from the published sources). The features limits, fallible_uint, cache
and bundled still exist. No change of the store format.

Applies after 0001 to 0004, against tag matrix-sdk-crypto-0.19.1 (commit
b18166c68bb958a21f0bca8b2d8320cb53583362). Not compiled locally (no Rust
toolchain on the workstation): the build workflow is the first compilation.

